      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Added a bounded local-flattening post-process after the Gaussian-RBF height-field fit. Around each contact the zero surface is made locally horizontal on a small disk and blended smoothly back into the fitted surface; disk radius, blend width and per-contact plateau heights are selected against the published objective. This raises the Euclidean distance from the zero surface to the labelled cells immediately above/below each contact and lowers the logistic/contact terms.",
        "parent_sha256": "043a8bb65cce42fb0b50a4a5159fb6342d36cf01eb8cf9993483a2007ba0482e",
        "rationale": "Round-1 measured 6.6373 (0 mismatches, contact RMSE 0.264). Diagnostics showed the remaining loss is dominated by contact logistic terms and the first label cell above/below each contact: surface tilt reduced their distances (e.g. nearest below-cell distance 0.67 instead of ~1). Flattening a small disk around each contact makes those distances near-vertical while a loss-guided search chooses the disk geometry and plateau heights, including contact bias. Local score improved reproducibly to 6.5171 with 0 mismatches, contact RMSE 0.2696, and ~30 s runtime, well inside the 120 s budget; public selfcheck still passes."
      },
